  "body": "There seems to be a spec bug in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#scroll-to-fragid\r\n\r\nIt still clears all the forward part of the history, even if the `replace` flag is set, because it does not mention the `replace` flag.  However, in chrome, it does handle the replace flag.  This can be easilly observed by running:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// get three urls in the history\r\nlocation.assign('#apple')\r\nlocation.assign('#bannana')\r\nlocation.assign('#cat')\r\n// go to middle history entry\r\nhistory.back();\r\n// replace the middle entry\r\nlocation.replace('#zebra');\r\n// go forward, spec says this is a no-op becuase replacing with `#zebra` cleared `#cat`\r\n// from the history. Actual result is that the url updates to `#cat`\r\nhistory.forward();\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese have to be pasted one at a time into the developer console, as the script will navigate the page.\r\n\r\ncc @domenic",
